@startuml
title UC-13 - Detect Application and Evaluate Rules (planned FST-027/FST-028)
autonumber
participant "Monitoring scheduler" as Monitor
participant "DetectDistractionUseCase" as Detect
participant "Session reader" as Sessions
participant "ActiveApplicationPort" as Apps
participant "OS adapter" as OS
participant "BlockingPolicyRepository" as Repo
participant "DistractionPolicyService + BlockingPolicy" as Policy
participant "Transactional outbox" as Outbox
participant "Outbox dispatcher" as Dispatch
participant "Log / progress / WebSocket" as Consumers
participant "BlockDistractionUseCase" as Block

Monitor -> Detect : tick(now)
Detect -> Sessions : current session and interval
Sessions --> Detect : state, interval type
alt RUNNING and WORK
  Detect -> Apps : currentApplication()
  Apps -> OS : read executable path / process name\nand transient instance identity
  OS --> Apps : observation or capability failure
  Apps --> Detect : application observation
  Detect -> Repo : findActive()
  Repo --> Detect : policy or none
  Detect -> Policy : evaluate application observation
  note right of Policy
    Pure evaluation; enabled rules only.
    Executable path before process name.
    Window-title patterns are deferred.
  end note
  Policy --> Detect : decision or no match
  alt enabled rule matches and detection is not debounced
    Detect -> Outbox : append DistractionDetected\n(detectionId, rule/target snapshot, action)
    Detect -> Outbox : commit detection transaction
    Dispatch -> Outbox : read committed events
    Outbox --> Dispatch : detection event
    Dispatch -> Consumers : deliver idempotently after commit
  else no policy / no match / duplicate log tick
    note right of Detect : No new detection event.
  end
  alt action BLOCK and target needs enforcement
    Detect -> Block : enforce detection / instance context
    ref over Block
      SD_BlockDistraction.puml
      Recheck eligibility before acting.
    end ref
  else action WARN
    Detect -> Consumers : request local learner warning
  else LOG / no match
    note right of Detect : No OS block operation.
  end
else paused / break / waiting / stopped
  note right of Detect : Do not collect a target or enforce a rule.
end
note over Apps, OS
  Platform selection and permissions: FST-027.
  Capability failure produces diagnostics, not a fabricated detection.
end note
note over Detect, Outbox
  Debounce suppresses repeated logs, not protection of a new instance.
  Enforcement never runs for an ignored/no-match observation.
end note
@enduml
